Validate checks the current environment against the code-owned ESHU_*
registry. It reports invalid values for known variables (errors),
deprecated variables (warnings), and unknown variables that resemble a
known name (likely typos). Use --strict to also flag every unrecognized
ESHU_* variable, and --reference to print the generated reference doc.

Usage:
  eshu config validate [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help        help for validate
      --reference   Print the generated environment-variable reference and exit
      --strict      Treat every unrecognized ESHU_* variable as a finding

Global Flags:
      --database string   Temporarily override database backend
  -V, --visual            Show results as interactive graph visualization
